content.text:
Add the design link in the README.md https://www.figma.com/design/eLY9H4h1aKQrDZg7XmPIHE/To-do-list-project?node-id=2-3&t=Fy2LShduijHFx3Si-0
The design is simple enough we can describe it.

The color pallete is monocromatic, we only have #1E1E1E and white.
CC3D3D is the picked error color.
Borders are 4 pixels and in our custom black.

Errors should appear inside a container with a 36px border radius  all in the picked error color with a white background.

The font is Inter, however for now we will use the browser font. Maybe later we will come back to this.

The main title has the following properties:
font-style: normal;
font-weight: 700;
font-size: 48px;
line-height: 58px;
text-align: center;
color: #FFFFFF;
vertical-align: middle;


The body text has the following properties:
font-weight: 400;
font-style: Regular;
font-size: 32px;
leading-trim: NONE;
line-height: 100%;
letter-spacing: 0%;
text-align: center;
vertical-align: middle;
color: #1E1E1E;


The main container in any given page has to be in a centered container with 18px border radius borders. There must be a custom black header with a centered title with 8px margin vertically.


The inputs have a 36px border radius border with a placeholder helper text inside.

This placeholder helper text has the following properties:
font-weight: 400;
font-style: Regular;
font-size: 32px;
leading-trim: NONE;
line-height: 100%;
letter-spacing: 0%;
text-align: left;
vertical-align: middle;
color: #1E1E1ECC (80% opacity).

Make sure the placeholder helper text has some breathing space in the left.

This are the logos we will use:




Given the fundations I will now describe the design:

In the todo list edit page, we must follow the main container standard where the main title is the name of list. In the body of the container a "Add your task…" input should be. In the leading position of the input the add button should be perfectly aligned to the right, inside the input!.  Below we will display the tasks, if not tasks we need to show a body text that says "No tasks have been entered yet". If there are tasks create we should show the task item. 

The task item has a leading circle of 48 px diameter with a custom black border. 20px later we have a task text and aligned to the right we have a delete button. If the task is completed we should strikethrough and we should use the checked icon.
The task text has the following properties:
font-weight: 400;
font-style: Regular;
font-size: 32px;
leading-trim: NONE;
line-height: 100%;
letter-spacing: 0%;
vertical-align: middle;
color: #1E1E1E;

For now, the title cannot be changed.

Following the same style the todolist index page, we should be able to add a todo list (just the list name), list the different lists, have a no lists caption, list the lists, click them to navigate to the edit page and destroy the lists (from this same index page).

Use as assets, inspirations and to validate the images in @tmp/images/

